<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="legendary-cloak">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_legendary_theblackprince.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Legendary Cloak for Fury Warrior</span></h2>In Phase 5, you can at last finish the Legendary Quest Line and earn your Legendary Cloak!<br/>
<br/>
<a class="q5 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=102249/gong-lu-strength-of-xuen">
<img alt="Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_cape_pandaria_tigermelee_d_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Gong-Lu, Strength of Xuen</span></a> is Fury Warriors' best alternative, offering our primary stat, Strength. Not only is the cloak 20 item-level higher than anything attainable from <a data-entity="zone" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/zone=6738/siege-of-orgrimmar">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Siege of Orgrimmar</span></a>, but it is also the only item in the game offering more than 2 secondary stats. Providing us with Hit, Crit, Haste &amp; Mastery.<br/>
<br/>This all in itself would've made the item insanely strong, but on top of that, it also has the proc <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146195/flurry-of-xuen">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/monk_stance_whitetiger.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flurry of Xuen</span></a>, causing you to deal AoE damage up to 5 mobs in front of you. It is to be noted that the proc can be a bit RNG, as it doesn't have an internal cooldown, but instead is RPPM (random proc per minute). From my own experience, this proc can be anywhere from 1-2% to 15% of your total damage output, depending on the encounter size and how often you can get it to proc during the encounter.<br/>
<br/>It's safe to say that your first priority going into Phase 5 of Mist of Pandaria Classic should be to attain the Legendary Cloak as quickly as possible.<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c1" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Fury Warrior Trinkets in Phase 5</span></h2>
<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Fury Warriors typically prefer running two passive trinkets. Sometimes we might use one on-use and one passive, but rarely ever two on-use. In the case of Phase 5 of Mists of Pandaria, we will default to our two standard passive trinkets, as there is no exceptional on-use trinket. <br/>
<br/>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<br/>There are no active trinkets of note worth mentioning for Fury Warriors, as all of our strongest trinkets are Passive Trinkets.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105491/evil-eye-of-galakras">
<img alt="Evil Eye of Galakras" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_11.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Evil Eye of Galakras</span></a> is by far and leagues better than any other option for Fury Warriors. This trinket is a must-obtain as it reduces the recovery rate of our talented abilities, such as <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=46924/bladestorm">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Bladestorm</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=107570/storm-bolt">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/warrior_talent_icon_stormbolt.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Storm Bolt</span></a>. It's especially strong for Fury Warriors, as it reduces the cooldown of Storm Bolt to 20 seconds, making it line up for each cast of <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=86346/colossus-smash">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_colossussmash.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Colossus Smash</span></a>. The trinket also provides an immensely strong Strength proc on an internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105609/thoks-tail-tip">
<img alt="Thok's Tail Tip" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Thok's Tail Tip</span></a> is generally your second-best trinket option in Phase 5. It increases your baseline Critical Strike damage and offers a Strength Proc on an internal cooldown.</div></li></ul>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=105459/fusion-fire-core">
<img alt="Fusion-Fire Core" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_orgrimmarraid_trinket_05.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fusion-Fire Core</span></a> is a very powerful trinket on AoE encounters. It's special as it has a chance to proc <a class="icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/spell=146136/cleave">
<img alt="" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_warrior_bladestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Cleave</span></a>, causing your attack to hit up to 5 extra targets. This trinket is going to be your second-best option on fights with 3 or more consistent targets, such as <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/1">Spoils of Pandaria </a> and <a data-contiguous="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/guide/1">Galakras</a>.</div></li></ul>
